1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,160
Hi. In this video, we'll look at techniques you can use in Burp Suite to identify which

2
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:15,520
parts of a token impact the response. Sometimes an application may only inspect

3
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:20,820
certain parts of a token. You can use the character frobber and bitflipper payload types

4
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:26,960
in Burp Intruder to modify the value of each character or bit position of a token in turn.

5
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:31,880
This enables you to identify which parts of the token impact the response you receive.

6
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:37,560
For example, if you modify the value of a character in a token and your request is still processed,

7
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:42,040
it is likely the character is not used. If you'd like to follow along to test out the

8
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:48,080
processes involved in this, you can use the lab Authentication Bypass via Encryption Oracle

9
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:54,160
from our Web Security Academy. We've already browsed around the site. Now we'll log in,

10
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:58,760
making use of the Stay Logged In option, and then log out again, so we have plenty of requests

11
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:01,800
in our proxy HTTP history tab.

12
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:10,400
The first step is to identify a message that includes a token that we want to investigate

13
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:16,560
further. In this case, we'll use the request for the My Account page when the user has enabled

14
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:24,200
the Stay Logged In cookie. To run the test, highlight the Stay Logged In cookie, right-click the message,

15
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:33,000
and select Send to Intruder. See that because we highlighted it, the cookie has been automatically

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,560
marked as a payload position. Under the Payloads tab, change the payload type to Character Frobber.

17
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:49,200
Click Start Attack. You can now review the results. We can see we have different status codes in

18
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:54,920
the responses, as the Character Frobber changes different parts of the cookie. So we can now

19
00:01:54,920 --> 00:02:01,920
analyze the responses to see the effect each change has had.

20
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:07,160
the

